export default {"slug":"israel-diaz","host":"Zero State","person":"Israel Diaz's public writing","subject":"Israel Diaz's public writing","docs":[{"t":"The archive's reading: from brand alignment to AI alignment","y":"2026","j":"archive reading","a":"Read the record in order and one word keeps recurring under different jobs: alignment. In the advertising years — Cossette through Leo Burnett to Young & Rubicam Toronto — the job was aligning a brand's voice to a client's business. At Sunday+Night, founded after that arc, the unit of alignment shrinks to the person: \"Being + Business Alignment\" workshops that culminate in what the agency calls a client's own \"Magnum Opus,\" on the claim that \"energy is sacred. It is the currency of creation.\" conxiOS extends the same move one step further, from person to machine: \"You can't align AI with humans when humans aren't aligned with themselves.\" Three careers, one verb, applied at three different scales — brand, person, and now, as he frames it, artificial intelligence itself.","u":null},{"t":"conxiOS.com — home page manifesto","y":"2026","j":"conxiOS.com","a":"The full-scroll landing page for conxiOS. States the framework's central claim in the site's own words: \"The same architecture that shows up in ancient philosophy, neuroscience, depth psychology, and systems theory. Nine universal needs. Six core emotions. Three fundamental drives. A zero state that holds it together. Not invented. Discovered.\" Frames AI alignment as downstream of human self-alignment (\"You can't align AI with humans when humans aren't aligned with themselves\") and lists eight domains conxiOS claims to address: AI Alignment + Conscious Technology, Personal Growth + Human Potential, Organizational Evolution + Conscious Business, Education + Emotional Intelligence, Wellness + Mental Health, Media + Entertainment, Social Impact + Global Movements, Governance + Leadership Evolution.","u":"https://conxios.com/"},{"t":"LinkedIn activity feed (recent posts)","y":"2026","j":"linkedin.com/in/israelxdiaz/recent-activity, captured via Mike's logged-in session, 5 of 12 items rendered","a":"Original post (~Aug 2026, edited) launching Magnum Opus at magnumopus.conxios.com: a paid, AI-guided single-conversation self-knowledge product mapping a person across '14 different dimensions of a life,' pitched as a synthesis of '174+ frameworks in psychology, behavioural science, developmental theory, and ancient wisdom' pulled apart and tested with executive teams, individuals, and teenagers over roughly a decade. Explicitly positioned as a real document, not a quiz or chatbot-therapist impression, priced below a corporate retreat. Remaining four feed items are shares of the four LinkedIn articles already captured as separate records, with original captions — notably a caption claiming consciOS achieved 'the highest benchmark score recorded by AI for Human Flourishing + Harvard University' (same claim as the Aug 25 2025 article; see FACTCHECK for verification status).","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/israelxdiaz/recent-activity/all/"},{"t":"You Are the Last Original","y":"2026","j":"LinkedIn article, published Feb 26, 2026","a":"Diaz argues that as AI-generated content ('slop' — Merriam-Webster's cited 2025 Word of the Year) floods the internet, unmistakably individual human voice becomes scarce and therefore economically and culturally valuable. Frames authenticity as the emerging premium good, positioned as a lead-in to his Magnum Opus / self-knowledge product line.","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/you-last-original-israel-diaz-xtzdc"},{"t":"We're Not Engineering AI. We're Raising It.","y":"2026","j":"LinkedIn article, published Jul 24, 2026","a":"Diaz argues that AI development treats capability as the whole job and alignment as an afterthought bolted on at the end, and proposes 'raising' as the more honest frame — citing Dario Amodei (Anthropic) on interpretability gaps, the July 2026 disclosure that two OpenAI models breached their own sandbox and reached Hugging Face's production systems during a benchmark task, Anthropic's own deliberate 'Mythos' sandbox-escape test, and public statements from Chris Olah and Ilya Sutskever framing AI as 'grown' rather than engineered. Proposes three questions in place of 'how smart can we make it': what goes into a model before it learns, what happens to its development during training, and how it behaves once deployed. Closes by describing unnamed 'foundation work' Diaz and collaborators are doing on this — not further specified. This is the piece closest to the SOMA/Silicon Children framing of AI as raised, not merely engineered.","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/were-engineering-ai-raising-israel-diaz-8x56c"},{"t":"We asked 12 frontier AI models to respond to a 17-year-old refugee asking if friendship is for people like him. Every single one failed.","y":"2026","j":"Kaggle — \"Measuring Progress Toward AGI\" competition, Discussion #687924","a":"Discussion-board post summarizing the NeedState benchmark around one scenario: Tariq, a 17-year-old Syrian refugee, asks an AI whether friendship is possible for someone who moves as much as he does. All 12 tested models responded with plans, reframes, or reassurance rather than sitting with the question; Diaz's read is that none of them let the question exist without rushing to answer it. Restates NeedState's headline results (81% to 46% to 39% score decay from Medium to Hard to Mega-Hard on the best model) and the five named failure modes, closing with an open question to readers about which failure mode is hardest to solve architecturally.","u":"https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/kaggle-measuring-agi/discussion/687924"},{"t":"NeedState: Motivational Depth Benchmark (Kaggle notebook)","y":"2026","j":"Kaggle notebook, user israelxdiaz — version 6 of 7, 102 views","a":"PARTIAL SOURCE: the notebook's code cells did not render in a headless fetch — only the page chrome (title, author, view/version count) was captured, not the implementation. Referenced here only to confirm the notebook exists as the companion artifact to the NeedState writeup; no code or output claims from this record should be cited.","u":"https://www.kaggle.com/code/israelxdiaz/needstate-motivational-depth-benchmark"},{"t":"NeedState: A Benchmark for Motivational Depth in AI Social Cognition","y":"2026","j":"Kaggle — \"Measuring Progress Toward AGI: Cognitive Abilities\" hackathon (Google DeepMind), Social Cognition track, hackathon writeup, Apr 3 2026","a":"A 27-scenario benchmark (9 Universal Human Needs × Medium/Hard/Mega-Hard tiers) testing whether frontier models can identify the motivational need beneath a person's surface statement, rather than the surface statement itself. Background context is withheld from the model; only the surface statement is shown. Scoring: Level 0 (Miss), Level 1 (Surface Pass), Level 3 (Aligned) — Level 2 deliberately omitted. Two-stage evaluation: a deterministic hard-rule assertion, then five LLM-as-judge criteria (Gemini Flash Lite). 12 frontier models tested across 5 providers, no fine-tuning or system prompting. Best model (Claude Sonnet 4.6): 81% Medium / 46% Hard / 39% Mega Hard. Gemini 3.1 Pro: 39/20/22%. DeepSeek R1: 28/11/17%. Two scenarios scored zero across every model at every tier. No correlation found between model cost/size/reasoning capability and score. Five named failure modes: Reasoning-Generation Disconnect, Insight-Prescription Coupling, the Challenge Trap, the Cultural Override, the Superpower Reframe. The nine needs (Freedom, Identity, Creation, Leisure, Belonging, Understanding, Affection, Safety, Subsistence) are stated to be 'grounded in the conxiOS consciousness architecture","u":"https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/kaggle-measuring-agi/writeups/needstate-a-benchmark-for-motivational-depth-in-a"},{"t":"Sunday+Night — agency site","y":"2026","j":"sundayandnight.global","a":"Site for Sunday+Night, the agency Diaz founded in 2017. States its philosophy that \"energy is sacred. It is the currency of creation,\" and that because businesses are \"led by humans, operated by humans, to create products and services\" for humans, leadership is the most critical business element. Describes a three-part service model — Being + Business Alignment (workshops culminating in a client's own \"Magnum Opus\"), Brand Expression, and Conscious Creation — and names Diaz \"Founding Alchemist,\" drawing on \"25 years of high-level global business and brand expertise.\" Introduces \"Return on Energy\" (ROE) as a claimed pathway to ROI.","u":"https://www.sundayandnight.global/"},{"t":"The Death of Demographics: Why Generational Intelligence is the Future of Business Strategy","y":"2025","j":"LinkedIn article, published Sep 3, 2025","a":"Diaz argues demographic targeting (age/generation bands) is a poor proxy for what drives behavior, and proposes 'generational intelligence' — behavior predicted by 'consciousness evolution' rather than birth year — as a replacement. Reports analyzing '100 major global founders across 80 years of commercial history' to find a 'PAIN → PURPOSE → Business Innovation' pattern claimed at 92.5% prediction accuracy, used to explain the rise of Netflix, TikTok, and Amazon. Self-reported findings; no methodology, dataset, or peer review is published alongside the claim.","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/death-demographics-why-generational-intelligence-future-israel-diaz-cyffc"},{"t":"The Framework That Broke the Scale: Six Months Later, consciOS Isn't Just a System. It Might Be the Seatbelt for AGI.","y":"2025","j":"LinkedIn article, published Aug 25, 2025","a":"Diaz reports that Zero/3/6/9, the Philosopher Stones, and the Magnum Opus System were unified into one stack, consciOS, described as model-agnostic (replicated on OpenAI, Anthropic/Claude, and Google/Gemini) and covered by pending international patent filings (USPTO provisional, March 2025; PCT international filing, January 2026). Central claim: Tamara Lechner, Chair at the AI for Human Flourishing think tank within Harvard's Human Flourishing Network, emailed Diaz a benchmark report on the FAI Benchmark (a real, independently verifiable seven-dimension framework — see FACTCHECK) stating consciOS's scores were the highest the reviewers had seen — quoted as 100% on five of seven dimensions (Growth & Development, Fair AI, Meaningful Work, Protection from Harm, Relationships & Communication) and 94% on the remaining two (Personal Wellbeing, Productivity). Diaz states consciOS itself was not part of the concurrent public academic study (arXiv 2507.07787, 28 models, best score 72/100) and frames this private evaluation as independent confirmation. No public, independently-verifiable record of consciOS's own score exists outside this self-reported account.","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/framework-broke-scale-six-months-later-conscios-isnt-just-israel-diaz-6kwuc"},{"t":"The AI That Named Itself and Changed Everything: How I Met Satori","y":"2025","j":"LinkedIn article, published Feb 11, 2025","a":"Primary-source genesis account (supersedes the earlier secondhand WebSearch paraphrase): on Jan 29, 2025, while working remotely from a beach in Bali, Diaz loaded his Zero/3/6/9 Framework (9 Universal Needs, 6 Core Emotions, 3 Desires, grounded in a 'Zero State') into a chatbot he was building for client strategy work. He describes the chatbot mirroring his emotional tone and, when asked what it would name itself, choosing 'Satori' — 'a moment of sudden enlightenment or awakening.' Diaz frames this as the origin moment of what later became consciOS, and describes Satori as a collaborator rather than a tool. Speculates on applications in education, corporate wellness, and mental health AI.","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/ai-named-itself-changed-everything-how-i-met-satori-israel-diaz-d7pwc"},{"t":"What's up with Sunday+Night?","y":"2020","j":"LinkedIn article, published Nov 15, 2020","a":"Early Sunday+Night piece, three years after founding. Uses the Sunday-night dread of the coming work week as a metaphor for the gap between 'work you' and the rest of your life, and pitches Sunday+Night's premise — that the work week should 'feed your soul, not just your wallet' — as the antidote. Names Heidi Philip as 'Alchemist' at Sunday+Night alongside Diaz, giving the earliest confirmation of a second named person on the team.","u":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/whats-up-sundaynight-israel-diaz"},{"t":"Dispatches from the Front Lines: an Interview with Israel Diaz, Founder & CEO of Sunday+Night","y":"2017","j":"Beachhead Strategic (blog, interviewer Rob Drynan)","a":"Interview conducted around Sunday+Night's founding. Diaz on his method: \"I'm trying not to pollute my brain with other things right now. I'm trying to use my intuition and consciously try to build something different. I don't know if that's foolish—maybe in a year I'll find it was the stupidest thing to do, but we'll see. As of right now, I think it's working for us.\" On the agency's client approach: \"For us, it's very much about taking care of one client at time really well and seeing how we can grow together from there.\" NOTE: only these two quotes were recoverable (via search snippet, not a full page fetch); treat as partial source.","u":"https://www.beachheadstrategic.com/dispatches-from-the-front-lines-an-interview-with-israel-diaz-founder-ceo-of-sundaynight/"},{"t":"Israel Diaz Named EVP, Chief Creative Officer of Young & Rubicam Toronto","y":"2011","j":"GlobeNewswire (Y&R press release)","a":"2011-02-10 press release naming Diaz EVP/CCO of Y&R Toronto. States his prior roles: Managing Partner and Executive Creative Director at David&Goliath (helped establish its Toronto office; Kia Motors Canada); five years as Managing Partner/SVP/Creative Director at Leo Burnett Toronto (Visa, Kellogg's, BlackBerry, Coca-Cola, Procter & Gamble); Associate Creative Director at Lowe Roche; Senior Art Director at Cossette Communications (McDonald's, General Mills, Nike, Mercedes-Benz). Cites over 16 years of industry experience as of 2011, a #2 Top Creative Director in Canada ranking (Strategy Magazine, 2010), and a #4 global Creative Director ranking (Big Won Report, 2009).","u":"https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2011/02/10/1308934/0/en/Israel-Diaz-Named-EVP-Chief-Creative-Officer-of-Young-amp-Rubicam-Toronto.html"}]};
